IMG Measures — Privacy Policy (For iPhone and iPad)
Last updated: 2026-11-19

Summary
IMG Measures does not collect, store on servers, share or sell any personal data. The app has no internet access and contains no advertising, analytics or tracking services.

Data on your device
The photos you take or import, your measurements, folders and settings are saved only in the app's own storage on your iPhone or iPad. From the photo metadata, the app only reads the orientation, to show the image the right way up, and, when an imported photo has no usable name, the date it was taken, to name the file. It does not read the location or any other metadata.

Permissions
Camera: the app asks for access to the camera only to take photos inside the app. Photos: photos are imported with the system photo picker, so the app only receives the photos you choose and does not need access to your library. Add to Photos: requested only when you save an annotated photo to the Photos app; the app adds the photo without reading your library. If you have already given IMG Measures full access to Photos, it is used only to find or create its “IMG_Measures” album. You can change these permissions at any time in the Settings app.

Exporting and sharing
Photos are only saved to the Photos app, PDF files are only saved to Files, and files are only shared with other apps through the share sheet when you choose to do so. From then on, they are handled by the app or service you choose, under its own privacy policy.

Backups
If iCloud Backup or a backup to your computer is turned on, the app's photos, measurements and folders can be included in your device backup and restored on a new device. Apple manages this process; you can turn it off in the Settings app.

Deleting your data
You can delete photos, measurements and folders inside the app at any time. Deleting the app from your iPhone or iPad removes everything it has stored on the device.

Children
The app does not collect personal data from anyone, including children.

Changes
If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page with an updated date.

